# Copy to .env for a local build, or set the variable inline in CI.
#
# PUBLIC_SITE_ORIGIN is the absolute origin the built site will be served from, with scheme and
# no trailing slash. It is the only thing that turns a preview build into a real one: canonical
# URLs, Open Graph URLs and any absolute link are built from it.
#
# THE DOMAIN IS grit.chat. Jason bought it; the registrar transfer completed 2026-08-25T00:16:37Z.
# An earlier revision of this file recorded it as undecided and surveyed gritchat.app, gritchat.io
# and gritchat.com. That was accurate then and is settled now.
#
# Leaving this unset still makes the build fall back to https://domain-not-chosen.invalid, a
# reserved host (RFC 2606) that can never resolve, so a preview build is obvious rather than quietly
# wrong. That guard is about forgetting to set the variable, not about the domain being unknown, so
# it stays.
#
# PUBLIC_SITE_ORIGIN=https://grit.chat
